      "code": "$profile = $profile + \"`n\" + \"Invoke-Mimikatz\";",
      "code_explain": "Concatenates a new line containing the literal string \"Invoke-Mimikatz\" to the $profile variable, which holds the path to the current PowerShell profile script. Modifying the profile is a classic persistence technique because the added line will run every time PowerShell starts, ensuring the Mimikatz function is loaded automatically.",
      "tag": "PERSISTENCE"
    },
    {
      "code": "Invoke-Expression $profile",
      "code_explain": "Executes the contents of the profile script immediately. By running Invoke‑Expression on the profile, the newly added \"Invoke-Mimikatz\" line is executed right away, triggering the credential‑dumping routine. Direct execution of arbitrary script text is a common abuse of PowerShell’s dynamic execution capabilities.",
      "tag": "CREDENTIAL_ACCESS"
    }
  ],
  "explain": "The script deliberately injects a call to Mimikatz—a well‑known credential‑dumping utility—into the PowerShell profile and runs it, providing both persistent execution and immediate credential extraction. These behaviors align with malicious activity rather than routine administration.",
  "is_malicious": "Malicious",
  "tag": "CREDENTIAL_ACCESS"
}

